                "headline": "Flood Warning issued August 11 at 6:06PM EDT until August 12 at 6:00AM EDT by NWS Charleston WV",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Athens County in southeastern Ohio...\nNorthern Meigs County in southeastern Ohio...\nSouthwestern Morgan County in southeastern Ohio...\nNortheastern Vinton County in southeastern Ohio...\nSouthwestern Washington County in southeastern Ohio...\nWest Central Wood County in northwestern West Virginia...\n\n* WHEN...Until 600 AM EDT Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Heavy rain has ended across the area. However, light to\nmoderate rainfall early this evening, in combination with runoff\nfrom the previous heavy rainfall, will result in continued flooding\nof mainly larger creeks and some rivers in the warned area.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 605 PM EDT, Doppler radar and area rain gauges indicated\nbetween 3 and 5 inches of rain has fallen since midnight last\nnight. People should remain vigilant tonight for lingering\nflooding of roads and low-lying locations.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nAthens, Belpre, Nelsonville, Albany, Coolville, Lake Hope State\nPark, Washington, Chauncey, Buchtel, Jacksonville, Trimble,\nStroud Run State Park, The Plains and Little Hocking.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nReport flooding to the National Weather Service by calling toll free,\n800 401 9535, when you can do so safely.",
